{"toolCallId":"call_9bcb07c2acf54ed6805957fe558ffe62","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"FILE_EXISTS | error  | Validates required spec documents for the declared documentation level.\nPLACEHOLDER_FILLED | error  | Rejects unfilled template placeholders in authored spec documents.\nCOMMENT_HYGIENE_MARKER | error  | Rejects ephemeral finding markers inside HTML comments in authored spec documents.\nSCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED | error  | Rejects scaffold-signature markers in required docs when spec.md claims Complete status.\nSTATUS_CROSS_DOC_CONSISTENCY | error  | Advisory-by-default check that spec.md and implementation-summary.md status fields classif\nLEVEL_DECLARED | info  | Reports whether the documentation level was declared or inferred.\nAC_COVERAGE | info  | Default-on advisory (non-blocking) scan for acceptance-criteria traceability coverage; set\nAC_CLOSURE | error  | Gates packet closure on acceptance-criteria.md at Levels 2, 3 and 3+; unmet criteria block\nANCHORS_VALID | error  | Checks anchors in each spec doc whose template defines them, ignoring fenced code; a phase\nFRONTMATTER_MEMORY_BLOCK | error  | Validates canonical _memory continuity frontmatter blocks.\nMERGE_LEGALITY | error  | Validates generated merge payloads against target anchor shape.\nSPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY | error  | Checks implementation-summary sufficiency after save/write flows.\nCROSS_ANCHOR_CONTAMINATION | error  | Detects route/category mismatches before generated content is merged.\nPOST_SAVE_FINGERPRINT | error  | Verifies post-save fingerprints for generated writes.\nTOC_POLICY | error  | Enforces table-of-contents placement policy.\nAI_PROTOCOLS | error  | Validates AI execution protocol sections in high-governance specs.\nCOMPLEXITY_MATCH | error  | Checks declared level against content complexity signals.\nFOLDER_NAMING | error  | Validates numbered spec-folder naming conventions.\nFRONTMATTER_VALID | error  | Validates YAML frontmatter structure and required semantic values.\nFRONTMATTER_VALUES | warn  | Warns when a packet document's contextType or importance_tier is outside the shared list i\nSOURCE_TAGS | warn  | Warns when a path:line citation inside a [SOURCE: ...] tag in a packet's research or revie\nGREP_CONVENTION | error  | Checks every markdown document in a spec folder against the greppable-corpus convention: f\nLEVEL_MATCH | error  | Checks required files match the declared documentation level.\nGRAPH_METADATA_PRESENT | warn  | Checks generated description and graph metadata are present.\nGRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_DRIFT | warn  | Flags graph-metadata.json children_ids missing on-disk phase children the writer would add\nGRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_IDENTITY | error  | Flags graph-metadata.json children_ids entries whose leading path identity is not the pack\nGRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE | warn  | Validates graph-metadata.json shape: required packet/derived blocks, last_active_child_id \nMETADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY | error  | Advisory-by-default check that description.json, graph-metadata.json, and continuity ids m\nDESCRIPTION_SHAPE | warn  | Validates description.json shape: required name/description/level keys present and well-ty\nNORMALIZER_LINT | error  | Strict-only lint for duplicated runtime normalizer helpers.\nSPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY | error  | Verifies inline markdown references resolve within spec docs.\nTEMPLATE_SOURCE | error  | Checks SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE provenance markers.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_ROOT_SPEC_REQUIRED | error  | Ensures canonical saves include a root spec reference.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_SOURCE_DOCS_REQUIRED | error  | Ensures canonical saves include source document references.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_LINEAGE_REQUIRED | error  | Ensures canonical save lineage metadata is present.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_PACKET_IDENTITY_NORMALIZED | error  | Checks canonical save packet identity normalization.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_DESCRIPTION_GRAPH_FRESHNESS | error  | Checks generated description/graph freshness for canonical saves.\nCONTINUITY_FRESHNESS | error | strict-only | Strict-mode freshness check for continuity frontmatter. The rule reports warn by default a\nGENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY | error | strict-only | Validates description.json and graph-metadata.json through the shared schemas plus path-pr\nGENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT | error | strict-only | Re-derives a folder and reports drift between the stored description/causal_summary and th\nLINKS_VALID | warn  | Scans the system-spec-kit skill's own markdown for wikilinks whose target file does not ex\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wff82223311/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"5097ba","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
